    "result_text": "The build passes. There is exactly one test class (`AcceptanceTest`), and it's green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `timezone` field derived from the owner's locality/region via the fixed region-to-timezone table.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `timezone` string property to the Owner schema (the DTO is generated from this spec at build time), documenting the derivation and the region\u2192IANA table.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added:\n   - `@Mapping(target = \"timezone\", expression = \"java(timezone(owner))\")` to `toOwnerDto`.\n   - A `REGION_TIMEZONE` map (`NSW\u2192Australia/Sydney`, `VIC\u2192Australia/Melbourne`, `QLD\u2192Australia/Brisbane`).\n   - A `timezone(owner)` method that looks up the owner's existing `locality(owner)` region in that table, returning `null` for regions with no known timezone (e.g. `UNKNOWN`).\n\nReusing `locality(owner)` keeps the timezone in lockstep with the already-derived region. The test `coreReturnsTimezoneForRegion` (postcode 2000 \u2192 NSW \u2192 `Australia/Sydney`) passes: **BUILD SUCCESS, Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0**.",
